{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"14b8b90f-0c4b-47b6-b2bf-3803814525db","agentId":"a31762a22e4ea769a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes, no searching. Memory limited: one 716px-wide CDP screenshot of the bench at the end (cleanup via cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py). Report under 120 words. Files: cuore/services/bench_bridge.py, cuore/web/bench_routes.py, cuore/web/templates/bench.html, cuore/live/checklists.py (+ cuore/api/checklists.py for the outcome field), cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py (next_action/readiness only), cuore/web/templates/_tools_panel.html (\"?\" rendering only), cuore/tests/check_bench.py. Do not edit base.html, _vbar.html, _vtabs.html, vehicle.html, feedback files, cuore.css (another agent). Spec: read C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\BENCH_UX_SPEC_2026-10-08.md sections A, B, C, D, H (items 1-11, 15, 18, 19, 20 except the \"?\" overlay). Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe; tests use a temp CUORE_STATE_DIR; VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115. Data: mes_bridge.workup (latest session/scan timestamps), faulttree.tree_for(code) via mes_bridge (steps with sources, inspect steps), known_good_bridge (expected readings), tools_kb_bridge (have status), cuore/live/store readiness observations, cuore/live/ops.status() (MES state, port), bench_bridge.build_bench, dossier_bridge.build_view.\n\nImplement: 1 Resume card at top (last scan relative time, changed since last visit = new codes/clears/records since the previous bench view time stored per VIN in state, \"N of M done\", the single next action). 2 Scan staleness on bench (hours since last scan; amber when > 24 h). 3 One display name per vehicle in every view's <title> (bench_bridge exposes it; title \"Bench · 1/3 · UNVERIFIED\"). 4 Each task expandable: procedure steps from the fault tree step (and electrical/physical inspect steps when the step has an element), referenced doc inline link (TSB entry text from mes.knowledge or the doc path), expected readings from known_good, and an explicit \"Pass = ...\" line; UNKNOWN stays honest. 5 Mark done captures an outcome: OK / fault found (+ one-line finding) / skipped (+ reason), with undo; stored on the checklist entry (extend checklists store and API: outcome, note); findings are also written as a mechanic note (mes.notes via mes_bridge) so they appear in history. 6 Shared parts/tools shown once at job level; per task only what differs. 7 Tools \"?\" placeholder replaced by have-status words (have / not owned / unknown: ask) in _tools_panel and the bench tools line. 8 Task states: READY (recommended), BLOCKED (reason), DONE; \"N of M done\". 9 Per-task preconditions with live status and a fix link (MES running for actuator tests: link /live; car connected: link /tools; fuel in window: text). 10 Fuel gate live: current fuel % from the last scan/live read, litres to burn to reach 85 % using tank capacity if sourced (mes.maintenance_specs/service_specs; else UNKNOWN), plus a readiness panel (monitors complete/incomplete from the latest from-car readiness observation, else \"no readiness read yet\"). 11 DTC chips link to the code page, title attr with meaning + status + which task addresses it, and a colour legend line. 15 \"Why\" expander labelled \"Why unverified?\" with the first basis line visible. 18 Real `<input type=\"checkbox\">` with a label \"Mark done: <task title>\" (or aria-pressed button) per row; one per visible task. 19 data-task-id and data-state on task rows. Checks (6): resume card present with \"last scan\" and \"of\"; a task expands to show \"Pass =\" and a procedure step; mark done with outcome \"fault found\" stores the note and shows DONE; preconditions show MES status; every task row has a labelled checkbox and data-task-id; title contains \"UNVERIFIED\". Run check_bench.py, check_dossier_view.py, check_api.py."},"uuid":"0f58c37e-26cd-4672-b8aa-6ae2cb6f1959","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:36:41.278Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
