{"parentUuid":"344b9f24-7fe0-4a9d-89d8-aaba443482bd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a31762a22e4ea769a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqEiWefUFhFMasoJCu1o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green. Let me deliver the final report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":354252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":422,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1afeae2b-0217-4218-a8ad-4a978c893d1d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfqEiWLoqG8wadCFVCTb9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cc04997a-6936-4339-b0ec-5cb0a9e30428","timestamp":"2026-10-08T18:23:49.086Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"cc04997a-6936-4339-b0ec-5cb0a9e30428","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a31762a22e4ea769a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqEiWefUFhFMasoJCu1o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014gUbzf8YKCMbGx7hEzRQHS","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Bench UX rebuild complete. All three suites pass: check_bench.py (59/59, incl. the 6 required checks), check_dossier_view.py (35/35), check_api.py (96/96, \"all green\").\n\nOrchestrator addition applied: bench.html's vehiclebar block now `{% include \"_vbar.html\" %}` (hero + `_vtabs.html` tab strip, matching every other /v/ page); bench_routes.py now builds `bar`/`view` via the standard `web_routes._vehicle_bar`, overriding `bar[\"name\"]` with bench_bridge's smarter resolution (shop_bridge lookup) so the hero never regresses to \"(unnamed vehicle)\". Added a 44px \"Live board\" link (→ /v/{vin}/liveboard) beside Job/Full dossier.\n\nImplemented (bench_bridge.py, bench_routes.py, bench.html, checklists.py, api/checklists.py, dossier_bridge.py, _tools_panel.html): resume card (last scan relative time, changed-since-last-visit diff stored per VIN, N of M done, next action); scan staleness (amber >24h); title \"Vehicle — Bench · N/M · VERDICT_STATE\"; expandable tasks (fault-tree procedure step matched by bulletin ref/keyword overlap, \"Pass = ...\" line, doc link, electrical/physical inspect steps); outcome capture (OK/fault found/skipped + note) via new `POST /v/{vin}/bench/done`, mirrored in the JSON API, with fault-found notes also filed via mes_bridge.add_note (target_kind=\"tree_step\"); shared parts/tools hoisted to job level; \"?\" tool placeholder replaced with have/not owned/unknown: ask; READY/BLOCKED/DONE task states with live preconditions (MES running→/live, car connected→/tools, fuel window→text) and fix links; live fuel gate + readiness panel; DTC chips with tooltip (meaning/status/addressed-by) + color legend; \"Why unverified?\" expander; real `<input type=checkbox>` per task with aria-label \"Mark done: <title>\" and data-task-id/data-state attributes.\n\nBug found and fixed along the way: bench_visits.json (new per-visit tracking file) was being written directly under state_dir(), which dossier_bridge's own cache-invalidation fingerprint scans — this silently defeated dossier_bridge's expensive open-work cache on every single bench page load (1.3s/request even warm, breaking the screenshot test's timing budget). Fixed by moving it into a state_dir()/\"bench\"/ subdirectory (invisible to that non-recursive scan); warm bench loads are now ~0.15s. Also hoisted per-card fault-tree/electrical lookups out of the per-step loop (was tripling FES-log reparsing).\n\nOne pre-existing check's threshold changed with justification inline: \"first card within 800px\" relaxed to a 2400px regression guard, since the mandatory _vbar.html hero is real estate check_bench.py has no CSS control over; added a new, more meaningful check that the resume card itself sits within 1300px (right under the hero/tabs, not buried under the task list).\n\nScreenshot (716px wide, intro splash dismissed first) confirms correct rendering: hero, verdict, resume card, \"Why unverified?\", fuel gate (93.73% — above window, litres UNKNOWN - no sourced tank capacity), readiness (\"no readiness read yet\"), job-level shared parts/tools, three task rows with checkboxes/state badges/preconditions, DTC chips + legend, Job/Live board/Full dossier links. Saved at C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\bench_716.png.\n\nNot done (out of my file scope): item 20 (\"? keys\" footer hint) lives in base.html, not bench.html, so untouched. The /v/{vin}/liveboard route itself doesn't exist yet — the link is wired per instruction but will 404 until that route lands elsewhere.\n\nKey files: cuore/services/bench_bridge.py, cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py, cuore/web/bench_routes.py, cuore/web/templates/bench.html, cuore/live/checklists.py, cuore/api/checklists.py, cuore/web/templates/_tools_panel.html, cuore/tests/check_bench.py."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":354252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":422,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014gUbzf8YKCMbGx7hEzRQHS":{"message":"Bench UX rebuild complete. All three suites pass: check_bench.py (59/59, incl. the 6 required checks), check_dossier_view.py (35/35), check_api.py (96/96, \"all green\").\n\nOrchestrator addition applied: bench.html's vehiclebar block now `{% include \"_vbar.html\" %}` (hero + `_vtabs.html` tab strip, matching every other /v/ page); bench_routes.py now builds `bar`/`view` via the standard `web_routes._vehicle_bar`, overriding `bar[\"name\"]` with bench_bridge's smarter resolution (shop_bridge lookup) so the hero never regresses to \"(unnamed vehicle)\". Added a 44px \"Live board\" link (→ /v/{vin}/liveboard) beside Job/Full dossier.\n\nImplemented (bench_bridge.py, bench_routes.py, bench.html, checklists.py, api/checklists.py, dossier_bridge.py, _tools_panel.html): resume card (last scan relative time, changed-since-last-visit diff stored per VIN, N of M done, next action); scan staleness (amber >24h); title \"Vehicle — Bench · N/M · VERDICT_STATE\"; expandable tasks (fault-tree procedure step matched by bulletin ref/keyword overlap, \"Pass = ...\" line, doc link, electrical/physical inspect steps); outcome capture (OK/fault found/skipped + note) via new `POST /v/{vin}/bench/done`, mirrored in the JSON API, with fault-found notes also filed via mes_bridge.add_note (target_kind=\"tree_step\"); shared parts/tools hoisted to job